From 357bfcab653b1a86a3130ee4d59445f0d1e0abbd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:42:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Arp: five fixed note orders, Converge, Diverge, Up & Down
 excl., Thumb and Pinky

New arp note modes after the existing ones (their numbers and saved names stay), for synths, MIDI, CV and the kit arp.
Each goes once through the notes held (in order of pitch), then on to the next octave as the octave mode says, as Up
does (modulation/arp_note_order.h):
- Converge: lowest, highest, 2nd lowest, 2nd highest, ...
- Diverge: from the middle outwards (Converge backwards)
- Up & Down excl.: up, then down without the top and the bottom note twice (Up & Down plays them twice)
- Thumb: the lowest note between each of the others, going up (C E C G C B)
- Pinky: the highest note between each of the others, going up (C B E B G B)
Saved as "converge", "diverge", "upDownExcl", "thumb", "pinky"; a firmware without them reads Up there. The kit arp's
menu leaves out Played Order and Pattern, so its options are mapped to the modes. 7-segment: CONV, DIVG, UPDX, THMB,
PNKY.
